WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.749 --> 00:00:03.807
- [Mark] All right, David?

00:00:03.807 --> 00:00:04.640
- Yeah.

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:05.481
- [Mark] David, where did you grow up?

00:00:05.481 --> 00:00:06.361
Where are you from originally?

00:00:06.361 --> 00:00:07.571
- Massachusetts.

00:00:07.571 --> 00:00:08.851
- [Mark] And tell me about your childhood,

00:00:08.851 --> 00:00:10.160
you had both of your
parents when you were a kid?

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:11.091
- [David] Yeah.

00:00:11.091 --> 00:00:12.708
- [Mark] How was your childhood?

00:00:12.708 --> 00:00:14.421
- [David] Not that happy.

00:00:14.421 --> 00:00:15.521
- [Mark] What kind of stuff went on?

00:00:15.521 --> 00:00:19.938
- It's my fault, oh, I had,
well, you know, problems.

00:00:22.459 --> 00:00:24.710
- [Mark] What do you, I
mean, what do you mean?

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:25.543
- Oh.

00:00:27.319 --> 00:00:28.309
(coughs)

00:00:28.309 --> 00:00:32.431
It's, I always felt like I didn't belong

00:00:32.431 --> 00:00:34.736
in certain groups.

00:00:34.736 --> 00:00:36.236
Always a misfit.

00:00:36.236 --> 00:00:37.069
- [Mark] Always a misfit.

00:00:37.069 --> 00:00:37.902
- Yeah.

00:00:37.902 --> 00:00:40.637
- [Mark] And what, tell me
about your parents, they were?

00:00:40.637 --> 00:00:44.137
- Oh Jesus, nice people, very nice people.

00:00:46.205 --> 00:00:48.441
I didn't treat them nice but.

00:00:48.441 --> 00:00:49.692
- [Mark] Were you adopted or-?

00:00:49.692 --> 00:00:50.923
- I'm adopted.

00:00:50.923 --> 00:00:52.048
- [Mark] You're adopted?

00:00:52.048 --> 00:00:52.881
- Yes.

00:00:52.881 --> 00:00:56.715
- [Mark] And, but no
traumatic events, nothing.

00:00:56.715 --> 00:00:59.951
It's more that you're,
you're the troublemaker?

00:00:59.951 --> 00:01:00.784
- Sort of.

00:01:04.186 --> 00:01:07.735
Some things were my
fault, maybe most of it,

00:01:07.735 --> 00:01:09.929
but I had my problems.

00:01:09.929 --> 00:01:11.574
- [Mark] Yeah, and what,
do you know anything

00:01:11.574 --> 00:01:13.875
about your blood, your parents?

00:01:13.875 --> 00:01:15.166
- None whatsoever.

00:01:15.166 --> 00:01:16.754
- [Mark] Nothing.

00:01:16.754 --> 00:01:18.822
And so what kind of kid
were you in high school?

00:01:18.822 --> 00:01:19.655
- What?

00:01:19.655 --> 00:01:21.644
- [Mark] What kind of kid
were you in high school?

00:01:21.644 --> 00:01:22.477
- Misfit.

00:01:24.016 --> 00:01:25.586
- [Mark] And so you went
on your own at what age?

00:01:25.586 --> 00:01:26.419
- Huh?

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:27.516
- [Mark] You went out
on your own at what age?

00:01:27.516 --> 00:01:29.767
- Yeah, when I was 17, 16, 17.

00:01:29.767 --> 00:01:30.619
- [Mark] Did you finish-

00:01:30.619 --> 00:01:31.696
- I got my GED.

00:01:31.696 --> 00:01:33.086
- [Mark] You did, okay.

00:01:33.086 --> 00:01:34.856
And where'd you go from there?

00:01:34.856 --> 00:01:38.523
- Oh, crappy job, one
crappy job to another.

00:01:41.274 --> 00:01:42.455
- [Mark] What kind of jobs you did?

00:01:42.455 --> 00:01:46.475
- Dish washing, I worked, um (coughs)

00:01:46.475 --> 00:01:48.806
I don't know if I can remember, (coughs)

00:01:48.806 --> 00:01:51.145
but I worked at Hayes
and Bickford's in Boston,

00:01:51.145 --> 00:01:52.895
they had these cafeterias.

00:01:52.895 --> 00:01:57.895
They're not around anymore,
them and Waldorf. (coughs)

00:01:58.195 --> 00:02:00.546
You remember Foxy's here in San Francisco?

00:02:00.546 --> 00:02:01.379
- [Mark] Don't.

00:02:01.379 --> 00:02:03.106
- They had a whole group of them.

00:02:03.106 --> 00:02:07.374
They were owned by the
way by the same people.

00:02:07.374 --> 00:02:10.267
It's kind of, (coughs) I
guess they went out of style.

00:02:10.267 --> 00:02:12.014
You know, these cafeterias.

00:02:12.014 --> 00:02:13.139
- [Mark] Right.

00:02:13.139 --> 00:02:15.988
- I know they don't have
them any around anymore.

00:02:15.988 --> 00:02:17.085
- [Mark] So do you have a family?

00:02:17.085 --> 00:02:18.003
Do you have kids of your own?

00:02:18.003 --> 00:02:19.497
- No, not that, no.

00:02:19.497 --> 00:02:20.330
- [Mark] Ever married?

00:02:20.330 --> 00:02:21.163
- No.

00:02:21.163 --> 00:02:22.666
- [Mark] Ever been in love?

00:02:22.666 --> 00:02:23.499
- Maybe.

00:02:26.333 --> 00:02:28.863
- [Mark] So you, have you
done prison time for anything?

00:02:28.863 --> 00:02:29.696
- No.

00:02:29.696 --> 00:02:30.994
- [Mark] Stayed out of
jail and prison stayed-?

00:02:30.994 --> 00:02:32.334
- I've been to jail, yes.

00:02:32.334 --> 00:02:33.835
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:02:33.835 --> 00:02:35.101
Are drugs a part of your life?

00:02:35.101 --> 00:02:35.934
- What?

00:02:35.934 --> 00:02:36.900
- [Mark] Are drugs a part of your life?

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:39.049
- No, (laughs) no.

00:02:39.049 --> 00:02:39.982
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:02:39.982 --> 00:02:41.747
- You're living here in the Tenderloin.

00:02:41.747 --> 00:02:42.580
- Yes.

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:43.822
- [Mark] In San Francisco,
you've been here since when?

00:02:43.822 --> 00:02:45.155
- 1981.

00:02:45.155 --> 00:02:45.988
- [Mark] It's a long time.

00:02:45.988 --> 00:02:46.821
- Yes.

00:02:46.821 --> 00:02:48.353
- [Mark] And you're staying
in one of the hotels now?

00:02:48.353 --> 00:02:51.474
- No, it's an apartment, it's
not a very nice apartment,

00:02:51.474 --> 00:02:53.458
but it's an apartment.

00:02:53.458 --> 00:02:55.466
- [Mark] And what do you do how
do you support yourself now?

00:02:55.466 --> 00:02:56.645
- I'm on (indistinct).

00:02:56.645 --> 00:02:58.108
- [Mark] So you're getting
money from the government?

00:02:58.108 --> 00:02:58.941
- Yeah.

00:02:58.941 --> 00:03:01.941
- [Mark] And were you ever homeless?

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:05.787
- Maybe at the longest
maybe a month at a time.

00:03:05.787 --> 00:03:06.620
- [Mark] Okay.

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:08.787
- And not very many times.

00:03:09.828 --> 00:03:14.828
- [Mark] So this, this misfit
outcast image that you have

00:03:15.066 --> 00:03:18.346
of yourself, do you think that came from,

00:03:18.346 --> 00:03:19.905
from anything that
happened in your childhood

00:03:19.905 --> 00:03:22.297
or was it maybe your blood parents or?

00:03:22.297 --> 00:03:25.434
- Maybe something I maybe
it's in my ancestry.

00:03:25.434 --> 00:03:27.154
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:03:27.154 --> 00:03:29.155
- [Mark] The fact that
you were adopted kind of-

00:03:29.155 --> 00:03:31.616
- Yeah, but I don't think that's it.

00:03:31.616 --> 00:03:32.783
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:03:34.017 --> 00:03:36.098
What's the most important lesson

00:03:36.098 --> 00:03:38.431
you've learned in your life?

00:03:39.372 --> 00:03:41.594
- (coughs) Oh, there's
a lot of them I guess.

00:03:41.594 --> 00:03:43.323
I've learned to keep my mouth shut.

00:03:43.323 --> 00:03:44.254
(Mark laughing)

00:03:44.254 --> 00:03:45.599
You can learn a lot.

00:03:45.599 --> 00:03:46.432
- [Mark] That's a good one.

00:03:46.432 --> 00:03:48.821
- I used to be, you know, kind of bud

00:03:48.821 --> 00:03:51.010
in people's conversations.

00:03:51.010 --> 00:03:53.388
Number one, they don't like it.

00:03:53.388 --> 00:03:58.388
Number two, you kind of keep
quiet, you can learn something.

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:02.051
That's very true I think. (coughs)

00:04:02.051 --> 00:04:03.639
- [Mark] Yeah, do you have friends?

00:04:03.639 --> 00:04:05.856
- Um, I have friends, yeah.

00:04:05.856 --> 00:04:09.189
Mainly from the soup kitchens I work in.

00:04:11.519 --> 00:04:13.089
- [Mark] Did you feel
like you were ever loved

00:04:13.089 --> 00:04:14.619
as a child or?

00:04:14.619 --> 00:04:16.536
- Not really, you know.

00:04:17.519 --> 00:04:20.218
Love is a strong emotion, but no.

00:04:20.218 --> 00:04:22.200
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:24.368
Is there anyone that you trust?

00:04:24.368 --> 00:04:26.238
- Oh, several people I trust, yeah.

00:04:26.238 --> 00:04:29.988
- [Mark] Yeah, that's
important to have, too.

00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:32.775
And are you happy?

00:04:32.775 --> 00:04:33.608
- Not really.

00:04:33.608 --> 00:04:34.441
- [Mark] No?

00:04:34.441 --> 00:04:35.941
- So-so, you know.

00:04:36.786 --> 00:04:38.977
I don't think, I don't
think most people are happy.

00:04:38.977 --> 00:04:41.498
- [Mark] No, I agree with that. (laughs)

00:04:41.498 --> 00:04:43.081
That's kinda what my channel's about.

00:04:43.081 --> 00:04:46.239
What, what do you think
gets in the way of that

00:04:46.239 --> 00:04:50.170
more than anything, for
yourself or for other people?

00:04:50.170 --> 00:04:52.290
- Just life itself I guess.

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:54.256
Trying to get along with other people.

00:04:54.256 --> 00:04:55.423
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:58.716
Do you wish you would had
done anything different

00:04:58.716 --> 00:04:59.549
about your life?

00:04:59.549 --> 00:05:00.466
- [David] Oh, yeah.

00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:01.807
- [Mark] Any regrets?

00:05:01.807 --> 00:05:03.548
- [David] I wish I'd
gotten, got a job, I know,

00:05:03.548 --> 00:05:06.465
lead a more regular life, you know.

00:05:07.481 --> 00:05:12.438
Maybe have a girlfriend, but
none that, that didn't work.

00:05:12.438 --> 00:05:16.311
- [Mark] What was the
best time of your life?

00:05:16.311 --> 00:05:20.252
- [David] Well, I mean,
in the early, in the 70s.

00:05:20.252 --> 00:05:21.912
- [Mark] What were you doing back then?

00:05:21.912 --> 00:05:23.984
- [David] (coughs) I
was on welfare, but um,

00:05:23.984 --> 00:05:26.769
I don't know, things worked for you.

00:05:26.769 --> 00:05:28.019
You met people.

00:05:29.999 --> 00:05:31.149
I had that three or four girls,

00:05:31.149 --> 00:05:34.732
it didn't amount to
anything, but you know.

00:05:36.222 --> 00:05:37.223
- [Mark] How old are you now?

00:05:37.223 --> 00:05:38.056
- [David] 74.

00:05:38.056 --> 00:05:39.056
- [Mark] 74.

00:05:42.168 --> 00:05:43.448
Do you see the world as a good place

00:05:43.448 --> 00:05:45.895
or do you see it as dangerous and

00:05:45.895 --> 00:05:49.062
if you know, how do you see the world?

00:05:50.699 --> 00:05:54.557
- [David] I think it's getting worse.

00:05:54.557 --> 00:05:55.917
(coughs)

00:05:55.917 --> 00:05:57.836
- [Mark] But people in
general, you see them as

00:05:57.836 --> 00:05:58.808
do you see people as good?

00:05:58.808 --> 00:06:01.597
- [David] I mean, you
look, I think we're growing

00:06:01.597 --> 00:06:03.858
back into fascism.

00:06:03.858 --> 00:06:08.180
Just look at the hitting
in Philippines, Brazil,

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:10.888
they even knocked Poland,
did you keep up with Poland?

00:06:10.888 --> 00:06:12.297
- [Mark] I don't.

00:06:12.297 --> 00:06:13.897
- (coughs) They had an election,

00:06:13.897 --> 00:06:16.026
it was some guy that was kind of a fascist

00:06:16.026 --> 00:06:18.449
but he lost out in the election.

00:06:18.449 --> 00:06:21.137
I think that was good news.

00:06:21.137 --> 00:06:22.697
Probably Russia, what else?

00:06:22.697 --> 00:06:26.656
All these countries, Hungary, (coughs)

00:06:26.656 --> 00:06:29.489
Philippines, Brazil, done with it.

00:06:30.827 --> 00:06:32.733
Do you ever keep up with
the news in these places?

00:06:32.733 --> 00:06:33.566
- [Mark] I don't.

00:06:33.566 --> 00:06:34.399
- Huh?

00:06:34.399 --> 00:06:35.457
- [Mark] I don't.

00:06:35.457 --> 00:06:39.525
- Oh, there's some more,
(coughs) Putin is a fascist.

00:06:39.525 --> 00:06:40.678
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:06:40.678 --> 00:06:41.761
- Definitely.

00:06:44.678 --> 00:06:47.456
- [Mark] And who you be
voting for this fall?

00:06:47.456 --> 00:06:50.887
- Oh, Biden, who are you probably?

00:06:50.887 --> 00:06:52.085
- [Mark] Yeah, I'm
probably not gonna vote,

00:06:52.085 --> 00:06:53.159
I'll just stay out of it.

00:06:53.159 --> 00:06:54.558
- Hm, well.

00:06:54.558 --> 00:06:58.445
- [Mark] Cause I'm in California,
so guess who's gonna win?

00:06:58.445 --> 00:07:01.684
- I think I unfortunately,
there's a good chance Trump will.

00:07:01.684 --> 00:07:02.517
- [Mark] Really?

00:07:02.517 --> 00:07:03.350
- Yeah.

00:07:03.350 --> 00:07:04.183
- [David] And not California, but-

00:07:04.183 --> 00:07:06.008
- Not California, but
the rest of the country.

00:07:06.008 --> 00:07:06.983
- [Mark] I'll be too busy editing

00:07:06.983 --> 00:07:09.436
to get off of my ass and vote.

00:07:09.436 --> 00:07:13.265
But, but you're happy here in California.

00:07:13.265 --> 00:07:15.222
Do you think just in general?

00:07:15.222 --> 00:07:18.773
- It's probably the only
place I can live in.

00:07:18.773 --> 00:07:20.164
- [Mike] You, you won't be
going back to Massachusetts?

00:07:20.164 --> 00:07:22.402
- No, no, no, no.

00:07:22.402 --> 00:07:24.875
Besides my sisters, she's adopted,

00:07:24.875 --> 00:07:27.504
but they live in the Maryland, anyway.

00:07:27.504 --> 00:07:28.483
I'm keeping track, but-

00:07:28.483 --> 00:07:29.462
- [Mark] That's nice.

00:07:29.462 --> 00:07:32.023
- But they live in Maryland, so.

00:07:32.023 --> 00:07:36.356
I don't think anybody I
know lives in Massachusetts.

00:07:37.371 --> 00:07:38.813
- [Mark] You ever, did you ever wanna get

00:07:38.813 --> 00:07:41.053
in touch with your actual parents?

00:07:41.053 --> 00:07:44.353
- [David] Um, I used to, I've
kinda given up, given that up.

00:07:44.353 --> 00:07:46.096
- [Mike] Yeah.

00:07:46.096 --> 00:07:47.233
- [David] They'd be dead by now.

00:07:47.233 --> 00:07:50.443
- [Mark] They're probably
not around now, yeah.

00:07:50.443 --> 00:07:51.276
All right, David, well,
thank you so much for talking

00:07:51.276 --> 00:07:54.896
with me and good luck with
whatever you do from here.

00:07:54.896 --> 00:07:55.729
- Alright.

00:07:55.729 --> 00:07:57.729
- [Mark] Thank you, man.

